  "security_implications": "This chunk directly drives kmac_data_o.data, which is likely a key/secret data bus to the KMAC engine. (1) Keys/secrets: The data selection among adv_data, id_data, gen_data with an error-induced decoy_data mask is intended to prevent secret leakage during faults. However, the security of this masking depends entirely on the non-secrecy of decoy_data and on error signals being asserted before secret selection. If decoy_data is tainted or error detection lags, secret could be output. (2) Wipe/clear: The block does not perform an explicit clear, but forces decoy_data on error, acting as a logical wipe of the output. The completeness of the error condition coverage must be verified externally. (3) Boundary/overflow: Index selectors (adv_sel, etc.) may be out-of-bounds if not constrained by the driving logic, leading to exposure of adjacent sensitive state. This is a high-concern area for key isolation.",
